  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 8 couples every same-colored structure across the board: the paired 9/7 controls reshape the upper carriage, 8/A reshape the lower carriage, and E simultaneously lowers the diamond carrier and extends the chamber's E arm. The central B glyph rotates the four-color chamber cross, and a remote move is globally blocked unless that color's chamber arm has clearance. Crucially, an arm aimed through the bottom opening may continue extending off-screen after its visible pixels reach row 62, allowing E to carry the diamond all the way to the lower socket.",
  "narrative": "Freshly replayed the resolver's exact 311-action prefix and confirmed frame.levels_completed=7. On Level 8, mapped both directional halves of the paired controls, rotated the chamber cross to make clearance for each coupled move, retracted the upper 7 span and lower A span to clear the diamond's x=18-20 lane, then pointed E through the chamber's bottom opening and extended it until the diamond reached the lower socket. The live run won Level 8 at action 382. A fresh reproduce() replay of the same 382-action full sequence reached claimed_level=8, completing the game's 8 win levels; total budget use was 311 live-prefix steps + 71 exploration/solve steps + 382 gate steps = 764.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Budget accounting is exactly 311 steps for the required live prefix, 71 further live Level-8 actions, and 382 steps for the successful fresh reproduction gate: 764 total.",
    "The large control boxes contain two directional click regions; for example, Level 8's 7 control uses approximately x=22 to retract the upper span and x=28 to extend it, while A uses x=9 to retract and x=15 to extend.",
    "The chamber cross's B rotation can require multiple repeated clicks to finish a 90-degree turn, and it cannot rotate while an arm remains extended through the bottom wall opening.",
    "To clear the top diamond lane, point chamber 9 through the bottom opening before raising the upper carriage enough to clear its wall stop, then retract 7 until the upper left column sits right of x=20.",
    "To clear the lower lane, point chamber 8 through the bottom opening, raise the lower assembly until its right column clears the isolated wall, then retract A until that column sits left of x=18; retract chamber 8 before rotating again.",
    "Visible screen bounds are not a collision boundary for the chamber arm: after E reaches row 62, further E clicks can show changes only in the remote top diamond until the win.",
    "Rejected clicks still consume the row-63 meter; compare rows 0-62 when deciding whether a mechanism actually moved."
  ],
